{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: none. The original program has no data block and no observed likelihood terms.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added explicit built-in uniform priors for `x_raw` and `y_raw`, matching their finite parameter constraints. This is density-neutral up to the same constant on the constrained support and satisfies SafeStan's requirement that every parameter have exactly one built-in prior sampling statement before use. The data file remains the empty JSON object.
","model_safe_stan":"/*
 * Hollow Square
 * http://www.openbugs.net/Examples/Funshapes.html
 *
 * Transform a uniform rectangle
 *    1234
 *    5678
 *    90AB
 * to a uniform hollow square
 *    1234
 *    5  6
 *    7  8
 *    90AB
 */
parameters {
  real<lower=0, upper=2> x_raw;
  real<lower=0, upper=1.5> y_raw;
}
model {
  x_raw ~ uniform(0, 2);
  y_raw ~ uniform(0, 1.5);
}
generated quantities {
  real x;
  real y;
  if (y_raw > 1) {
    // cases 1, 2, 3, 4
    x = x_raw - 1;
    y = y_raw - 0.5;
  } else if (y_raw < 0.5) {
    // cases 9, 0, A, B
    x = x_raw - 1;
    y = y_raw - 1;
  } else if (x_raw < 0.5) {
    // case 5
    x = x_raw - 1;
    y = y_raw - 0.5;
  } else if (x_raw < 1.0) {
    // case 6
    x = x_raw - 1.5;
    y = y_raw - 1;
  } else if (x_raw < 1.5) {
    // case 7
    x = x_raw - 0.5;
    y = y_raw - 0.5;
  } else {
    x = x_raw - 1.0;
    y = y_raw - 1.0;
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{}","protected_variables":[]}
